    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived attribute following the repository's established pattern for derived owner fields (pure logic in `OwnerDerivations`, a thin `@Transient` getter on `Owner`, and an OpenAPI schema property that MapStruct auto-maps into `OwnerDto`).\n\nThree edits:\n\n1. **`OwnerDerivations.java`** \u2014 added `ownerSegment(int membershipLevel, String locality)`: TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when the locality is a known region else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (whose keys are exactly NSW/VIC/QLD) as the canonical known-region set, so `UNKNOWN` correctly yields `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `@Transient getOwnerSegment()` getter that feeds in `getMembershipLevel()` and `getLocality()`, mirroring the other derived getters.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it by name into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\nBoth spec cases verified end-to-end: a known-region owner at membership level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and an unknown-region owner \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
